1.text:
The five exemplars are all C V C

* 2nd letter  ∈ { a , u , o }
* 3rd letter ∈ { d , b , t , w }

dad = d a d , dab = d a b , gut = g u t , low = l o w , cat = c a t

satisfy C a/u/o C with a final d/b/t/w.  The five non-exemplars fail the
requirement, e.g.  ear, cop, ego, mom, ate all break the V / C3
condition.

In the set

* leg = l e g       V = e ∉ {a,u,o} and 3rd = g ∉ {d,b,t,w}
* dam = d a m       V = a ok but 3rd = m ∉ {d,b,t,w}
* rat = r a t       V = a and 3rd = t – the only option that meets the
  C a/u/o C / d,b,t,w requirement
* car = c a r       V = a ok but 3rd = r ∉ {d,b,t,w}
* bin = b i n       V = i ∉ {a,u,o}

so, up to the usual wording, the only member of the list that does meet
the dad/dab/gut/low/cat pattern is rat.  In particular leg is a clear
non-member, 2nd letter e and 3rd letter g being outside the required
sets.  The same is true of dam, car and bin.

